## Control {{controlId}}: Limit Access to CUI on System Media to Authorized Users

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization limits access to CUI on system media within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through role-based access control, sensitivity labels, and device configuration restrictions managed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.

{{#if dlpLabelsConfigured}}
**Sensitivity-Based Access Control:**
{{dlpLabelsCount}} sensitivity labels enforce access restrictions on CUI media:
{{#each labels}}
- **{{name}}**{{#if isActive}} (Active){{else}} (Inactive){{/if}} — Priority: {{priority}}
{{/each}}

Labels restrict access to authorized users only, preventing unauthorized viewing, copying, or forwarding of labeled content.
{{else}}
Sensitivity label access controls have not been configured.
{{/if}}

{{#if cuiGroupExists}}
**CUI Authorization:**
The "{{groupDisplayName}}" security group ({{memberCount}} members) defines the authorized population for CUI media access. Only group members can access CUI-labeled content.
{{/if}}

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
**Removable Media Restrictions:**
{{deviceConfigurationsCount}} device configuration policies restrict USB and removable media access:
- USB storage blocked or restricted to read-only on managed endpoints
- Removable media requires encryption before CUI transfer
- External storage device access logged for audit purposes
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine sensitivity label access policies, CUI group membership, device USB restriction configurations, and removable media access logs.

